  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Activate the third player – 2v2 becomes 3v2",
  "description": "Both teams attack the same goal with a goalkeeper. Each team has two players on the rink and a third player – the back – at the centre line, with the rest of the team in a line behind. The drill starts 2v2 when the goalkeeper passes the puck out.\n\nA team may only score once it has activated its third player: the puck is played up to the back at the centre line, who moves it on first time and joins the game. That makes it 3v2. If the team with two players wins the puck, they in turn must find their back at the centre line – then it is 3v3 and both teams may score.\n\nA shot that does not score: the shooter goes back to the line, and the team is down to two on the rink again. After a goal both teams restart 2v2 from the goalkeeper. The drill keeps switching between 3v2 and 2v3: in attack it is about using the extra player and finding the best shot, in defence about standing up to the pressure and finding the way up to your own back. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look for your back early – without them you cannot score."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "In 3v2: draw the defenders and pick the best shot, not the first one."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "In 2v3: press the player on the puck and close the pass up to the other team's back."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "When you win the puck: find your own back straight away."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
